WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9194763Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9205886Z ^[[0m
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9206695Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9207276Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9207666Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9208571Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9209170Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9209604Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9209996Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9210644Z    if you are ready to continue.
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9210993Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9211437Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9211886Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9212319Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9212613Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9212751Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9212892Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9213121Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9213295Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9213637Z    can use Nix.
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9213758Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9213844Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9213976Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9214219Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9214624Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9214870Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9215156Z I will:
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9215313Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9215470Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9215783Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9216162Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9216512Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9216745Z  - install Nix in /nix
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9216967Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9217290Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9217591Z    /root
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9231244Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9231760Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9240122Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9240476Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9241845Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9242049Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9242286Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9257328Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9257689Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9265930Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9266403Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9266674Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9266780Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9266884Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9267024Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9267130Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9267434Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9267627Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9267694Z If you would like to
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9267835Z see the output, try like this:
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9267933Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9268029Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-13T07:40:50.9268239Z   $ sh ./install-nix
